*Must-read: China AI Bulletin
<https://substack.com/redirect/27c8deed-40ca-4a68-8192-1b70eeb52b55?j=3DeyJ=
1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E>*

For the Safe AI Forum, Emmie Hine provides biweekly updates on AI
development, governance, and safety in China. This was an extremely
informative and insightful issue, including summaries of 88
AI-safety-related papers published by Chinese researchers as well as
coverage of MIIT=E2=80=99s standardization effort for the Model Context Pro=
tocol.
*Must-read: China=E2=80=99s Agentic AI Controversy
<https://substack.com/redirect/e2cdfa32-9d2f-493d-a745-69eef6daa163?j=3DeyJ=
1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E>*

Samm Sacks=E2=80=99s *Lawfare *piece unpacks the uproar around ByteDance=E2=
=80=99s Doubao
AI phone. She finds that the AI agent (embedded into the phone=E2=80=99s op=
erating
system) has =E2=80=9C*sparked a flurry of discussion among China=E2=80=99s =
legal scholars
and technologists about how regulators should address the unprecedented
challenges agentic AI poses to data security and privacy*.=E2=80=9D This re=
port is
chock-full of references that I will be coming back to, including many
links to commentaries from Chinese scholars.
*Should-read: The Trade War Lab
<https://substack.com/redirect/96f9dc43-85f2-415f-ba9e-53204a7ffa3e?j=3DeyJ=
1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E>*

Based at the University of Kansas, the Trade War Lab aims to decode the
US-China trade war =E2=80=9Cfrom the bottom up.=E2=80=9D It=E2=80=99s a ver=
y cool model that brings
together undergraduate and graduate students with faculty mentors to
conduct research. For instance, this issue examines China=E2=80=99s support=
 for
liberal order enforcement (sanctions) based on UN Security Council voting
data.
*Should-read: My Tesla Was Driving Itself Perfectly=E2=80=94Until It Crashe=
d
<https://substack.com/redirect/56afdecd-4048-4c79-a1f6-fd42dc80d65a?j=3DeyJ=
1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E>*

In *The Atlantic*, the former head of Uber=E2=80=99s self-driving car divis=
ion,
Raffi Krikorian tries to piece together what went wrong with his own
accident while operating a Tesla in full self-driving mode.
*Should-read: A Signal Point of Failure: Integrating BeiDou into U.S.
Positioning, Navigation, and Timing Systems
<https://substack.com/redirect/c90c931b-9ead-43ef-ab05-c1f0e1b07388?j=3DeyJ=
1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E>*

While doing some research into the rise of devices that can receive signals
from multiple global navigation satellite systems, I stumbled upon this *Wa=
r
on the Rocks* op-ed by Jesse Humpal, a former NSC staffer in the Biden
administration. These days, it=E2=80=99s rare to come across a genuinely cr=
eative
policy idea: =E2=80=9C*integrating China=E2=80=99s BeiDou satellite navigat=
ion system as a
backup for civilian use to enhance redundancy and interoperability across
the private sector, including in critical infrastructure*.=E2=80=9D
*Should-read: China Rolls Out Interim Regulations on AI Human-Like
Interaction Services: A Detailed Analysis
<https://substack.com/redirect/4d471d70-a6d9-48fc-9d26-c31d6105ae11?j=3DeyJ=
